Subject: [PATCH] server: Preserve the desktop close timer for the manager's own threads.

If the last application exits while explorer is still initializing, removing
its desktop user schedules WM_CLOSE. Explorer then starts its clipboard,
display-settings or COM threads. Attaching those threads used to cancel the
timer, leaving explorer and the Wine services alive with no application left.

Only a thread from another process should cancel an already scheduled close.
The desktop manager's own threads do not add another application using it.

Reproduced in Wine 11.0 directly on Linux and inside Boxedwine by cancelling
Notepad while explorer initializes. Regression coverage exercises the actual
server/winstation.c timer code in probes/test_desktop_close_timer.py.

--- a/server/winstation.c
+++ b/server/winstation.c
@@ -431,7 +431,8 @@ static void add_desktop_thread( struct desktop *desktop, struct thread *thread )
     if (!thread->process->is_system)
     {
         desktop->users++;
-        if (desktop->close_timeout)
+        /* The manager's own startup threads must not keep an unused desktop alive. */
+        if (desktop->close_timeout && thread->process != get_top_window_owner( desktop ))
         {
             remove_timeout_user( desktop->close_timeout );
             desktop->close_timeout = NULL;
